712 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 442 0 R
/E (LLMs are not inherently designed for tasks like counting or repetitive arithmetic, which can lead to infinite loops or inconsistent results. For instance, if an agent responsible for passport control in an airport must count individuals, relying on the LLM for counting may result in errors. Instead, delegate repetitive mathematical tasks to simple programming constructs \(e.g., a Python loop\) and use context variables to pass sequential data to the LLM. This division of labor helps maintain accuracy and efficiency. In my LangGraph training I am building a Passport Control for an Airport with Vision Models and I show case this.)
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
