772 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 450 0 R
/T (when should you use AI Agents?)
/E (when should you use AI Agents?)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
773 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 450 0 R
/E (AI agents are particularly effective for complex, open-ended tasks where the number of steps cannot be predetermined and flexibility is essential. They are well-suited for scenarios requiring dynamic decision-making, such as customer support interactions and coding tasks, where the agent can autonomously plan and execute actions based on real-time feedback. However, it's crucial to balance their autonomy with appropriate guardrails and thorough testing to mitigate risks associated with higher costs and potential error accumulation. In contrast, for tasks that can be clearly defined and decomposed into fixed subtasks, implementing structured workflows with predefined code paths may be more efficient and cost-effective. Read Anthropic view on this.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
